The code completes the `showToast` method and implements a `queueToast` method in the `Utils` class. 
1. **`showToast`**: It creates a `Toast` widget, adds a label with the provided text, and attaches a `TableShowHideListener`. This listener ensures that if a toast is already visible, it is hidden when a new one appears. When the toast is hidden, it checks the `toastQueue` to see if another toast should be displayed. Finally, it sets the `currentToast` reference and shows the toast on the `foregroundStage`.
2. **`queueToast`**: This method follows a similar logic to `showToast` but adds the toast to the `toastQueue` instead of showing it immediately. If no toast is currently active (`currentToast == null`), it triggers `showToast` to start the sequence.

